MMC block: write lock from the device tree. A host node with
gemba,writable-sectors (pairs of 32-bit cells: start and count, in 512-byte
sectors) locks its card: every write, discard, secure erase or write-zeroes
request not wholly inside one range fails, as does any other write-direction
driver request, and the MMC_IOC_CMD and MMC_IOC_MULTI_CMD ioctls are refused
(a read-direction command can still erase or lock the card). Requests reach
mmc_blk_mq_issue_rq with absolute card sectors, CQE or not. The boot loader
sets /chosen gemba,unlocked when it boots the stash or recovery; the card is
then unlocked. MMC_BLOCK_WRITE_LOCK (default y) builds the lock.

--- a/drivers/mmc/core/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/Kconfig
@@ -46,6 +46,15 @@ config MMC_BLOCK
 	  mount the filesystem. Almost everyone wishing MMC support
 	  should say Y or M here.
 
+config MMC_BLOCK_WRITE_LOCK
+	bool "Card write lock from the device tree"
+	depends on MMC_BLOCK && OF
+	default y
+	help
+	  Refuses card writes outside the gemba,writable-sectors ranges of
+	  the host node, and the MMC ioctls, unless /chosen has
+	  gemba,unlocked.
+
 config MMC_BLOCK_MINORS
 	int "Number of minors per block device"
 	depends on MMC_BLOCK
